From-source: wasm_compilation_experiments/exp1_re2/absl-wasm.patch
Purpose: lets absl::base::GetNumCPUs compile for wasm32-wasi.

abseil-cpp's sysinfo.cc final branch calls
`std::thread::hardware_concurrency()`, which isn't available under
wasm32-wasi (no <thread> in the non-threads sysroot).  Add a
`__wasm__`/`__wasi__` short-circuit that returns 1 (single-threaded
execution model).

--- a/absl/base/internal/sysinfo.cc
+++ b/absl/base/internal/sysinfo.cc
@@ -148,6 +148,9 @@ static int GetNumCPUs() {
   return hardware_concurrency ? hardware_concurrency : 1;
 #elif defined(_AIX)
   return sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN);
+#elif defined(__wasm__) || defined(__wasi__)
+  // No threading on wasm32-wasi (single-threaded execution model).
+  return 1;
 #else
   // Other possibilities:
   //  - Read /sys/devices/system/cpu/online and use cpumask_parse()
